<title>UK: RUSSIA NOVOROSSIISK PORT OPEN AS SWELL SUBSIDES.</title>
<headline>RUSSIA NOVOROSSIISK PORT OPEN AS SWELL SUBSIDES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's main oil export terminal of Novorossiisk on the Black Sea reopened early on Thursday after a 16-hour shutdown due to a heavy swell, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port was shut at 1340 local on Wednesday and operations were suspended until 0600 on Thursday because of the waves.</p>
<p>One large crude tanker was alongside berth one with a second waiting at anchor outside the port.</p>
<p>Other oil ports on the Black Sea and Baltic were open and working normally, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
